    "parsing_res_list": [
        {
            "block_label": "header",
            "block_content": "Part 11A General fees rules ",
            "block_bbox": [
                161,
                30,
                449,
                50
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 99A ",
            "block_bbox": [
                157,
                115,
                309,
                137
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Part 11A-General fees rules ",
            "block_bbox": [
                157,
                186,
                658,
                221
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "99A Application ",
            "block_bbox": [
                155,
                275,
                375,
                301
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The rules set out in this Part do not apply to self managed.superannuation funds.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                295,
                329,
                933,
                379
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "99B No entry fees ",
            "block_bbox": [
                153,
                412,
                390,
                439
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) The trustee, or the trustees, of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund must not charge entry fees..",
            "block_bbox": [
                245,
                466,
                1021,
                519
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(2) An entry fee is a fee, other than a buy-sell spread, that relates,directly or indirectly, to the issuing of a beneficial interest in a superannuation entity to a person who is not already a member of the entity.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                245,
                542,
                1025,
                652
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "99BA No exit fees ",
            "block_bbox": [
                149,
                690,
                386,
                713
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) The trustee, or the trustees, of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund must not charge exit fees, except in circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
            "block_bbox": [
                242,
                742,
                1018,
                823
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(2) An exit fee is a fee, other than a buy-sell spread, that relates to the disposal of all or part of a member's interests in a superannuation entity.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                242,
                847,
                1025,
                926
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "99C Buy-sell spreads and switching fees to be charged on a cost recovery basis \n",
            "block_bbox": [
                147,
                962,
                972,
                1016
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) If the trustee, or the trustees, of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund charge a buy-sell spread or a switching fee, the fee must be no more than it would be if it were charged on a cost recovery basis.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                242,
                1042,
                1025,
                1148
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(2) The regulations may prescribe the way in which a buy-sell spread or a switching fee charged on a cost recovery basis is to be worked out.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                244,
                1172,
                1020,
                1249
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 13
        },
        {
            "block_label": "number",
            "block_content": "332",
            "block_bbox": [
                155,
                1321,
                186,
                1337
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "footer",
            "block_content": "Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993",
            "block_bbox": [
                435,
                1321,
                817,
                1339
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
